.SH NAME
le-fix-terminal - Undo terminal modes a killed TUI left behind


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle fix-terminal [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Undo the terminal modes a TUI leaves behind when it is killed without
getting to clean up — mouse reporting, bracketed paste, a hidden cursor,
the alt screen. Symptoms are a prompt that fills with \fB;62;38M65;…\fR
whenever the mouse moves, a missing cursor, or a terminal that stays
blank after a crash.

.PP
Every sequence it writes is idempotent, so running it on a healthy
terminal does nothing. Do not redirect its output — the escapes have to
reach the terminal to have any effect.

.PP
\fBreset\fR does this too, and also clears your scrollback.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fix-terminal


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


